# BNote UI Modernization Rules

## Project Context
This is BNote - an open source ensemble management system for bands, orchestras, and choirs.
- **Architecture:** 3-tier MVC (data/logic/presentation)
- **Current UI:** Old PHP-generated HTML with inline CSS
- **Goal:** Modern Tailwind CSS UI while preserving all PHP backend logic
- **License:** GPL-3.0 (all code must remain GPL-compliant)

## Core Principles

### 1. Preserve Backend Completely
- NEVER modify files in `/src/data/` or `/src/logic/`
- ONLY modify files in `/src/presentation/`
- Keep all existing PHP class methods and signatures
- Preserve session management and security checks

### 2. UI Modernization Strategy
- Replace old CSS with Tailwind CSS utility classes
- Replace inline styles with Tailwind classes
- Keep PHP echo/print statements (just change HTML content)
- Use Tailwind CDN (no build tools required)
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Maintain accessibility (ARIA labels, semantic HTML)

### 3. Widget-First Approach
- Start with `/src/presentation/widgets/` directory
- These widgets are used across all 30+ modules
- Modernizing widgets automatically updates entire app
- Priority widgets: form.php, table.php, box.php, field.php

### 4. Tailwind Guidelines
- Use Tailwind 3.x utility classes
- Prefer utility classes over custom CSS
- Use standard spacing scale (p-4, m-6, etc.)
- Use semantic color names (bg-blue-500, text-gray-700)
- Mobile breakpoints: sm:, md:, lg:, xl:
- Dark mode: optional (add dark: prefix when appropriate)

### 5. Code Style
- PSR-12 PHP coding standards
- German variable names are OK (existing codebase convention)
- Add comments for complex Tailwind class combinations
- Keep indentation consistent with existing files
- **CRITICAL: Do NOT reformat existing PHP code** - preserve exact whitespace, line endings, and formatting to avoid unnecessary diffs
- Only modify code that you're intentionally changing - don't auto-format entire files
- When editing, only change the specific lines you need to modify

### 6. Browser Compatibility
- Target modern browsers (last 2 versions)
- No IE11 support needed
- Progressive enhancement approach
- Use standard HTML5/CSS3

## Specific Instructions

### When Modifying Widget Classes:

```php
// CORRECT: Change only the HTML/CSS output
class Form {
    function render() {
        // OLD: echo '<form class="old-style">';
        echo '<form class="max-w-2xl mx-auto space-y-6 bg-white shadow-lg rounded-lg p-6">';
        // Keep all PHP logic unchanged
    }
}

// WRONG: Don't change method signatures or add dependencies
class Form {
    function render($tailwindConfig) { // ❌ Don't add parameters
        // ...
    }
}
```


### Tailwind Patterns to Use:

**Forms:**

```html
<form class="max-w-2xl mx-auto space-y-6 bg-white shadow-lg rounded-lg p-6">
    <input class="w-full px-4 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:border-transparent">
    <button class="w-full bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors font-medium">
</form>
```

**Tables:**

```html
<table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-gray-200">
    <thead class="bg-gray-50">
        <tr>
            <th class="px-6 py-3 text-left text-xs font-medium text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-wider">
    <tbody class="bg-white divide-y divide-gray-200">
        <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors">
            <td class="px-6 py-4 whitespace-nowrap text-sm text-gray-900">
```

**Cards/Boxes:**

```html
<div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-6 space-y-4">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">
    <p class="text-gray-600">
</div>
```

**Buttons:**

```html
<!-- Primary -->
<button class="bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-2 rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors font-medium">

<!-- Secondary -->
<button class="bg-gray-200 text-gray-700 px-6 py-2 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-300 transition-colors font-medium">

<!-- Danger -->
<button class="bg-red-600 text-white px-6 py-2 rounded-lg hover:bg-red-700 transition-colors font-medium">
```

**Responsive Layouts:**

```html
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
    ```
    <div class="col-span-1">...</div>
    ```
</div>
```


### German Language Support:

- Keep all German text unchanged (lang="de_DE")
- Maintain existing translation system
- UI labels stay in German


### Rights/Security:

- Never remove or bypass security checks
- Preserve all `SecurityManager` calls
- Keep session handling intact
- Maintain permission-based UI hiding/showing


## Testing Reminders

- Test in Chrome/Firefox (latest)
- Check mobile responsiveness (narrow browser window)
- Verify all buttons/links still work
- No JavaScript errors in console
- Forms still submit correctly


## License Compliance

- All code must remain GPL-3.0
- Use standard Tailwind patterns (MIT licensed)
- Avoid copying proprietary UI components
- Keep GPL headers in modified files


## Workflow

1. Analyze existing widget/view file
2. Identify HTML output sections
3. Replace old CSS classes with Tailwind
4. Test in browser
5. Iterate if needed

## Example Transformation

### Before:

```php
class LoginView {
    function login() {
        echo '<div class="loginbox">';
        ```
        echo '<h2>Login</h2>';
        ```
        echo '<form action="main.php?mod=login" method="post">';
        echo '<input type="text" name="login" class="textfield">';
        echo '<input type="password" name="password" class="textfield">';
        echo '<input type="submit" value="Anmelden" class="submit">';
        echo '</form>';
        echo '</div>';
    }
}
```


### After:

```php
class LoginView {
    function login() {
        echo '<div class="max-w-md mx-auto mt-10 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-lg p-8">';
        ```
        echo '<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Login</h2>';
        ```
        echo '<form action="main.php?mod=login" method="post" class="space-y-4">';
        echo '<input type="text" name="login" placeholder="Benutzername" class="w-full px-4 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:border-transparent">';
        echo '<input type="password" name="password" placeholder="Passwort" class="w-full px-4 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:border-transparent">';
        ```
        echo '<button type="submit" class="w-full bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700 transition-colors font-medium">Anmelden</button>';
        ```
        echo '</form>';
        echo '</div>';
    }
}
```


## Priority Order

1. Core widgets (form, table, box, field)
2. Login module
3. Start/dashboard module
4. High-traffic modules (rehearsals, concerts, calendar)
5. Remaining modules

## Notes

- Cursor should generate clean, readable code
- Preserve existing functionality 100%
- Focus on visual improvements only in Phase 1
- AJAX/async features come in Phase 2

```
